# Stage "main": everything needed to decide the PR's design.
#
# Expand with `node scripts/make-stage.mjs main` (writes stages/main.steps and
# prints the estimate), then start it with
#   printf 'sha=%s\nsteps=stages/main.steps\n' <sha> > markers/READY-main
# Directives (lines starting with @) are documented in scripts/make-stage.mjs.
# Every measuring step is resumable (--if-missing): a rerun after a failure
# skips what already finished.
#
# Order: the core picture first, so that a stage cut short still answers the
# main questions: prepare, the full matrix (2 rotations), the combination copy
# of the screened survivors (variants/combo.patch, prepared up front by the
# first step; tiers 1 and 2), the extras and their reports, and only then the
# variant confirmation: every survivor in variants/survivors.json `order`
# (design candidates first, the clear wins in screening order, the borderline
# survivors last) in batches of 3 next to main/branch/main-aa, rotations 0-5,
# scale 0.5, on the batch's targets plus the tier 1 guard T1G (tier 1 at
# XS/x64/x1 and the tier 1 headline entries), all at XS/S/C/x64/x1.
#
# Subsets: the runtime and JIT-tier extras run HD (the headline subset plus
# every tier 1 data-first entry) instead of the full tier 1 subset, the
# pollution profiles G1/G2/G10 at C and M, the loaders the headline subset H.

